opennyai_summary.facts:
2. For the sake of convenience, the parties are referred to herein as per their status before the Tribunal.
3. Brief facts of the case are as follows:
That on 08.12.2007, the petitioner was proceeding in the motor cycle bearing registration No.KA-19/V-747 as a pillion rider from Manipal towards Mangalore.
The said motor cycle was driven in a rash and negligent manner by its rider which resulted in an accident and the petitioner sustained the following injuries:-
"1. Lacerated wound 4x1 cm. x bone deep, horizontally, between two eyebrows with underlying fracture of frontal bone, bilateral nasal bones medial wells of both orbits;
2. Lacerated wound 7x 2 cm. extending from the right inner cheek over the nose to reach just inner to left eye with underlying fracture of nasal septum, both maxillary sinuses and zygomatic process of maxilla on left side;
3. Full thickness lacerated wound 7 x 1.5 cm. over right side of the face involving the right upper lip;
4. Fracture of the mandible;
5. Multiple small lacerated wounds over the tongue with loss of front one third of the tongue;
6. Loss of the lower right central incisor, canine 1st premolar and 2nd prelomar and lower left central incisor, lateral incisor, canine and 1st premolar teeth;
Mr Preetham Saldanha vs Richard W Saldanha S/O Pascal Saldanha on 17 January, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/42326981/
